  "provenance": "All source values derive from the pinned Sanytron factory firmware binpackage (RS30_HAOS_HA100_V1.0.4_20260702). source_members are the binpackage images as shipped (system/vendor/cache are Android-sparse); restore_images are the full-partition images the factory restore actually flashes, produced by expanding the sparse members and padding every image to its exact device partition size. The preloader and every calibration/identity partition are preserved and never written. The restore /data is a fresh empty F2FS sized to the partition (the factory userdata member is only a placeholder), so it has no reproducible content hash and is verified structurally by its two F2FS superblocks. Nothing here redistributes firmware bytes: the installer fetches the archive from the vendor Drive source and trusts only these repo-pinned hashes."
